    stem: "The circles u and v represent two wheels that are free to rotate about their centres, as shown. The radius of u is 4 cm and the radius of v is 6 cm.",
    questionText: "(i) Find the length of the circumference of each circle. Give your answers in cm in terms of π. (ii) The wheels u and v are in non-slip contact and therefore the rotation of one causes the other to rotate. Find the number of complete rotations wheel u makes if wheel v completes 100 rotations.",
