    stem: "A company makes and sells fibre optic cable. It can sell, at most, 200 kilometres of cable in a week. For a certain range of its production the company has found that profit can be modelled using the function: P(x) = 275x − x² − 2000, where x ≤ 200. In the function, x is the number of kilometres of fibre optic cable sold and P(x) is the profit in euro.",
    questionText: "In a particular week the company made a profit of €8350. Find the number of kilometres of cable it sold that week.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"questionTotal"}, totalMarks: 10,
